# =============================================================================
# ghl-leadflow-demo — .gitignore
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything committed is immediately visible to
# anyone. Treat sanitization as mandatory, not optional.
#
# NOTE: *.json is deliberately NOT ignored. n8n workflow exports and example
# payloads are versioned JSON artifacts of this project. Credential-shaped
# JSON is denied by specific patterns below instead of by a blanket rule.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets and environment ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Credentials, keys, service accounts ------------------------------------
# Specific patterns only, so legitimate project JSON is never swallowed.
service-account*.json
*service-account*.json
*-credentials.json
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
gcp-*.json
gha-creds-*.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
*.ppk
.netrc
.git-credentials

# --- Local-only documentation -----------------------------------------------
# Full, unsanitized environment inventory. Never publish.
docs/environment.local.md
*.local.md

# --- Captured webhook payloads ----------------------------------------------
# GHL's free Outbound Webhook action supports no headers, so the shared secret
# travels INSIDE the body. Every payload captured from a real delivery is
# therefore secret-bearing.
#
# DENY EVERYTHING, then allow back only the redacted example fixtures. An
# earlier version ignored `*.local.json` and `captured*.json` by naming
# convention, which meant a capture saved as `payloads/tc03.json` was
# committable. Naming discipline is not a control; this is.
payloads/*
!payloads/*.example.json

# --- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
jspm_packages/

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# --- Test output, coverage, artifacts ---------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
playwright/.auth/
.last-run.json
# Playwright MCP scratch: page snapshots and console logs of a live CRM session.
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Tunnel config ----------------------------------------------------------
# ngrok config files hold the authtoken.
ngrok.yml
ngrok.yaml
.ngrok2/

# --- n8n local state --------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime data, database, and encryption key. Workflow EXPORTS under
# workflows/ are intentionally versioned and are not matched here.
#
# WARNING: `n8n export:workflow --decrypted` writes credential values in
# cleartext. Never use it for anything destined for this repository. A secret
# typed directly into a node parameter — rather than bound to an n8n
# credential — is included in EVERY export form. Bind secrets to credentials.
.n8n/
n8n-data/
n8n_data/
.n8n-local/
database.sqlite
database.sqlite-*
*.n8n.encryptionkey

# --- Local agent/tool config ------------------------------------------------
# These can carry env blocks with tokens. .claude/settings.json (project
# permissions, no secrets) is intentionally NOT ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
.mcp.json
.cursor/mcp.json

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
.cache/
.tmp/
tmp/

# --- OS and editor ----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

# --- Cloud-sync conflict artifacts ------------------------------------------
# Sync conflicts produce duplicate files whose names would otherwise be
# committed by accident. Note the gap: a hostname-suffixed conflict copy
# cannot be matched generically without also swallowing legitimate hyphenated
# filenames. Stage explicit paths and read `git status --short`; never
# `git add .` in this repository.
*conflicted copy*
* - Copy.*
* (1).*
* (2).*
*.tmp
~$*
.tmp.drivedownload/
.tmp.driveupload/

# Local agent config — never committed
.claude/

# Local agent registry cache — generated by local tooling, not project state
.atl/
